Wrote `labels/coder-2.json`. HB 1447 gave Donato both a sponsor act and a Yea vote establishing a school-library removal-request chapter (parent or community member may request removal of obscene/harmful material, reviewed by the governing body), but the same act bundles unrelated education provisions (Muncie schools flexibility, vendor-survey privacy, political neutrality, obscenity-dissemination criminal law), so it's `multi-subject` with no Donato statement tying her support to the library clause — coded BLANK `no-evidence`.
